WEBVTT

00:00:10.900 --> 00:00:11.450
Um...

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:12.660
What?

00:00:13.410 --> 00:00:16.420
Are Kent and the others... all right?

00:00:16.910 --> 00:00:18.470
They weren't made to sortie.

00:00:18.910 --> 00:00:20.250
The Infinity is doing well, too.

00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:22.750
I... see...

00:00:23.970 --> 00:00:24.630
Damn it!

00:00:27.780 --> 00:00:29.610
They were too optimistic in their assessment of the situation!

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:36.890
Sora wo aogi Hoshi yo michite Tobitatsu no Asu e no brilliant road

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:36.890
Look up to the sky, rise to the stars, Take-off on the brilliant road of tomorrow

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:36.890
空を仰ぎ 星よ満ちて 飛び立つの 明日への brilliant road

00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:44.840
Kokoro no aosa Kono te ni daite go far away

00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:44.840
Carry the unexpierence of the heart in the hands and go far away

00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:44.840
心の蒼さ この手に抱いて go far away

00:00:55.860 --> 00:00:59.940
Urayamu koto ni Narete shimattara

00:00:55.860 --> 00:00:59.940
If you have experienced the envy

00:00:55.860 --> 00:00:59.940
羨む事に 慣れてしまったら

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:05.970
Hokoreru jibun ga Toozakatteku

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:05.970
Your proud self will go far away

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:05.970
誇れる自分が 遠ざかってく

00:01:08.130 --> 00:01:13.140
Mienai tsubasa de habataku no fly higher

00:01:08.130 --> 00:01:13.140
Flapping the invisible wings to fly higher

00:01:08.130 --> 00:01:13.140
見えない翼で羽ばたくの fly higher

00:01:14.350 --> 00:01:20.470
Yume wo egaku no wa hito ni umareta kara

00:01:14.350 --> 00:01:20.470
I'm imaging dreams because I was born a "person"

00:01:14.350 --> 00:01:20.470
夢を描くのは「人」に生まれたから

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:24.580
Sora wo aogi Hoshi yo michite

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:24.580
Look up to the sky, rise to the stars,

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:24.580
空を仰ぎ 星よ満ちて

00:01:24.580 --> 00:01:28.040
Tobitatsu no Asu e no brilliant road

00:01:24.580 --> 00:01:28.040
Take-off on the brilliant road of tomorrow.

00:01:24.580 --> 00:01:28.040
飛び立つの 明日への brilliant road

00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:32.920
Kokoro no aosa Kono te ni daite

00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:32.920
Carry the unexperienced of the heart in the hands

00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:32.920
心の蒼さ この手に抱いて

00:01:34.090 --> 00:01:40.850
Anata to nara Yowai jibun wo sarakedashite hashiridaseru no

00:01:34.090 --> 00:01:40.850
If I were with you, I'd start running, exposing my weak self

00:01:34.090 --> 00:01:40.850
あなたとなら 弱い自分をさらけ出して走り出せるの

00:01:41.090 --> 00:01:48.540
Mirai yo dou ka Mugen ni tsuzuke go far away

00:01:41.090 --> 00:01:48.540
The future! Somehow continues to the infinity, go far away

00:01:41.090 --> 00:01:48.540
未来よどうか 無限に続け go far away

00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:05.890
Episode Seventeen: 
Battle

00:02:02.540 --> 00:02:04.290
I can't believe that we're bringing Infinity's generators... 

00:02:04.290 --> 00:02:06.420
...on such a slow ship.

00:02:07.400 --> 00:02:08.700
They'll give it three times the maneuverability...

00:02:09.340 --> 00:02:11.650
...and let it fly like the Katies.

00:02:12.060 --> 00:02:15.930
But if they don't get there in time, then they're meaningless.

00:02:17.260 --> 00:02:19.950
I wonder if there's... anything I can do.

00:02:20.930 --> 00:02:21.800
We're going to start.

00:02:23.740 --> 00:02:25.130
We're going to attach the laser pods.

00:02:26.140 --> 00:02:27.900
You can at least configure the settings, right?

00:02:32.790 --> 00:02:34.550
Take him away once his pulse stabilizes.

00:02:34.730 --> 00:02:35.130
Yes, ma'am!

00:02:35.970 --> 00:02:37.040
Everyone, listen for a second!

00:02:37.650 --> 00:02:39.080
Anyone that's relatively free...

00:02:39.380 --> 00:02:41.090
...help us make the emergency room!

00:02:41.350 --> 00:02:41.810
Yes, ma'am!

00:02:45.280 --> 00:02:47.910
I'm sorry. We came to help, but...

00:02:49.070 --> 00:02:50.200
It's all right.

00:02:51.070 --> 00:02:52.630
Please tell my wife...

00:02:53.380 --> 00:02:55.460
...that going on vacation is looking impossi...

00:02:56.440 --> 00:02:59.020
Your wife will be just as happy to hear that you're fine...

00:02:59.740 --> 00:03:00.870
...so do your best.

00:03:01.680 --> 00:03:02.490
Right...

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:14.080
The fleet's organization was very ill-prepared.

00:03:15.040 --> 00:03:19.140
In the end, no one imagined that a real fight would occur.

00:03:20.620 --> 00:03:22.360
You didn't, and neither did I.

00:03:22.870 --> 00:03:23.390
Yes...

00:03:24.380 --> 00:03:27.470
With the remaining firepower, we are limited in what we can do.

00:03:28.510 --> 00:03:29.440
It's going to be an all-out battle.

00:03:31.060 --> 00:03:33.230
Get the students to sortie, too.

00:03:35.160 --> 00:03:35.800
Roger.

00:03:39.650 --> 00:03:40.840
All-out battle...

00:03:42.710 --> 00:03:43.850
It's easy to say.

00:03:47.890 --> 00:03:48.810
A battle...

00:03:50.030 --> 00:03:51.240
What we have to do is the same.

00:03:52.020 --> 00:03:53.960
We're putting what we've learned into practice...

00:04:02.920 --> 00:04:04.760
Is it all right to fiddle with it so much?

00:04:05.060 --> 00:04:07.830
Yeah. I'm just removing the unnecessary parts, after all.

00:04:08.190 --> 00:04:10.410
I have to make the system lighter, even a little...

00:04:10.930 --> 00:04:12.610
...because this will be meaningless...

00:04:12.730 --> 00:04:15.330
...if the information processing can't keep up with your reaction speed.

00:04:16.570 --> 00:04:17.930
No matter what...

00:04:18.540 --> 00:04:20.100
...let's save Rinna's father and the others.

00:04:20.480 --> 00:04:20.880
Yeah...

00:04:21.430 --> 00:04:22.120
No matter what.

00:04:26.580 --> 00:04:27.850
Ah, wait a second!

00:04:29.930 --> 00:04:32.480
Please use the Bianca's fittings this time!

00:04:33.170 --> 00:04:34.390
Can you do that?

00:04:34.850 --> 00:04:36.810
The durability is also higher.

00:04:37.480 --> 00:04:39.900
If you adjust the length, you can use it, so please do!

00:04:40.200 --> 00:04:40.940
She says.

00:04:42.310 --> 00:04:44.510
The Bianca's...
M3 line!

00:04:45.200 --> 00:04:46.040
Get that ready!

00:04:47.510 --> 00:04:49.600
You certainly do understand this well...

00:04:49.800 --> 00:04:50.450
Yeah...

00:04:51.420 --> 00:04:52.850
When you're in a situation where you can't...

00:04:52.920 --> 00:04:55.090
...get supplies and maintenance to your satisfaction...

00:04:56.220 --> 00:04:59.480
The construction sites for all of the space stations are like that.

00:05:00.640 --> 00:05:03.070
Didn't you used to be a pilot before this?

00:05:03.360 --> 00:05:03.880
That's right.

00:05:06.280 --> 00:05:08.100
And quite an exceptional one, too.

00:05:09.090 --> 00:05:13.360
However... it ended at a point in time when I thought that I was excellent.

00:05:14.030 --> 00:05:15.570
I was full of myself.

00:05:18.450 --> 00:05:20.830
I thought I could do anything by myself.

00:05:24.790 --> 00:05:26.550
This is low of you, Miss Machida!

00:05:35.400 --> 00:05:36.380
Let me see that.

00:05:36.900 --> 00:05:37.970
There isn't much time.

00:05:41.070 --> 00:05:45.720
In the end, I got sent to a station in an undeveloped region of space.

00:05:46.680 --> 00:05:47.890
I got demoted.

00:05:48.730 --> 00:05:50.680
In one turn, an elite pilot got sent to the bottom.

00:05:50.960 --> 00:05:53.740
I lost my temper, I got depressed, I drank, and I got into fights.

00:05:54.480 --> 00:05:57.010
Then one day, there was an accident on the station.

00:06:02.520 --> 00:06:05.410
While I saved one person, dozens of other people died.

00:06:06.690 --> 00:06:07.870
That's when I understood...

00:06:09.060 --> 00:06:12.060
...that a person's power is trivial.

00:06:13.220 --> 00:06:14.440
However, Machida...

00:06:25.340 --> 00:06:28.840
It's no use. No matter how many times we try, we can't open the locks.

00:06:29.390 --> 00:06:30.310
I see...

00:06:31.040 --> 00:06:32.290
I wonder what's going on.

00:06:32.830 --> 00:06:36.820
They've taken over our systems, yet they aren't attacking.

00:06:37.400 --> 00:06:39.130
We can't do anything if we can't get out.

00:06:39.770 --> 00:06:40.870
What do they want?

00:06:42.050 --> 00:06:43.500
The Cosmic Fracture...

00:06:43.870 --> 00:06:44.370
What?

00:06:45.000 --> 00:06:48.390
If the enemy's goal is the Cosmic Fracture, then...

00:06:49.980 --> 00:06:54.200
If they're letting us analyze the Fracture's data...

00:06:54.540 --> 00:06:56.050
...then their goal is...

00:07:08.400 --> 00:07:08.860
Number three?

00:07:09.210 --> 00:07:11.720
Yeah. Erase it completely.

00:07:14.870 --> 00:07:16.030
Then the next one is...

00:07:16.520 --> 00:07:17.590
You're removing more of them?

00:07:17.790 --> 00:07:18.170
Yeah.

00:07:19.090 --> 00:07:21.060
All of the functions we don't use very much.

00:07:21.750 --> 00:07:22.420
Are you worried?

00:07:22.590 --> 00:07:23.770
Er, um, no...

00:07:29.130 --> 00:07:33.290
If Kouta can fly Infi the way he flew his Bianca back then...

00:07:38.440 --> 00:07:39.780
Mom, um...

00:07:40.230 --> 00:07:40.840
What is it?

00:07:41.710 --> 00:07:44.710
I'll do my best to help Miss Ren and the others during this time.

00:07:45.290 --> 00:07:48.210
If I do, do you think Dad will forgive me?

00:07:48.790 --> 00:07:49.830
It'll be all right.

00:07:50.610 --> 00:07:53.790
But I promised him that I'd go get him.

00:07:54.460 --> 00:07:57.630
But it would be better for me to help here, right?

00:07:58.160 --> 00:07:59.640
I'm a kid, after all...

00:08:00.390 --> 00:08:01.570
This is frustrating.

00:08:09.090 --> 00:08:10.160
Hey, hurry it up!

00:08:10.480 --> 00:08:11.060
Right!

00:08:13.140 --> 00:08:15.420
The head of the maintenance staff got mad at me.

00:08:16.090 --> 00:08:16.980
What did you say?

00:08:17.620 --> 00:08:20.510
I said that we would help, since we're students.

00:08:21.060 --> 00:08:24.790
And he said, "Right now, you're pilots, and this is just before you sortie..."

00:08:25.110 --> 00:08:26.640
"Standing by is your job, too."

00:08:26.900 --> 00:08:28.100
"Be sure to rest."

00:08:28.440 --> 00:08:29.400
Exactly.

00:08:31.960 --> 00:08:32.920
A sortie...

00:08:34.160 --> 00:08:35.720
We haven't done that since the Great Mission...

00:08:36.420 --> 00:08:37.240
That's true.

00:08:37.980 --> 00:08:40.520
But... this is a whole different thing.

00:08:54.900 --> 00:08:57.320
All Katies have finished their preparations for launch.

00:08:58.110 --> 00:08:59.960
We are beginning our rendezvous with the Strelka.

00:09:10.800 --> 00:09:13.460
The battle... is going to begin, isn't it?

00:09:14.330 --> 00:09:15.770
I'm scared, too.

00:09:16.380 --> 00:09:17.390
Everyone is.

00:09:28.010 --> 00:09:29.160
This is an all-out battle...

00:09:29.540 --> 00:09:31.650
We're having all of the students sortie, too.

00:09:32.460 --> 00:09:34.280
A time like this is why they were brought along.

00:09:34.950 --> 00:09:36.160
I know that.

00:09:36.770 --> 00:09:37.870
But I'm skeptical...

00:09:39.200 --> 00:09:40.320
All we can do is believe in them.

00:09:41.050 --> 00:09:42.060
That's true.

00:09:46.450 --> 00:09:48.420
Would you take care of attaching the generators for me?

00:09:48.850 --> 00:09:49.370
Got it.

00:09:49.780 --> 00:09:51.800
Yo, Leila Barthes!

00:09:51.950 --> 00:09:53.940
Oh... Juno Mayol!

00:09:55.040 --> 00:09:57.210
That's right, I'm Juno Mayol!

00:09:57.990 --> 00:09:59.030
Long time, no see.

00:10:00.070 --> 00:10:00.540
Who's this?

00:10:01.110 --> 00:10:02.490
If you let him use manipulators...

00:10:02.560 --> 00:10:04.320
...then he's the greatest man in the Sol System.

00:10:04.820 --> 00:10:05.680
Commander!

00:10:06.750 --> 00:10:08.550
Please let me help with something!

00:10:09.180 --> 00:10:11.000
At this rate, I won't be able to settle down!

00:10:12.250 --> 00:10:13.980
Manipulators...

00:10:14.790 --> 00:10:16.060
Generators...

00:10:19.040 --> 00:10:21.280
Thanks! I owe you one!

00:10:21.530 --> 00:10:22.370
Same here!

00:10:22.890 --> 00:10:24.510
We're counting on you, Juno!

00:10:27.660 --> 00:10:30.440
I had heard that you had become an instructor, but...

00:10:31.010 --> 00:10:32.260
I'm dealing with it somehow.

00:10:33.040 --> 00:10:34.890
For now, let's start with a meeting.

00:10:35.240 --> 00:10:35.930
All right!

00:10:36.310 --> 00:10:36.970
There's no time.

00:10:37.260 --> 00:10:38.290
There's a room over there.

00:10:45.730 --> 00:10:46.770
We've been waiting for you.

00:10:47.790 --> 00:10:49.320
Things have gotten out of hand, haven't they?

00:10:52.120 --> 00:10:53.370
I'll do my best.

00:10:54.180 --> 00:10:56.720
So that I... don't hold everyone back...

00:11:03.570 --> 00:11:05.480
We'll configure the settings and attach the parts at the same time.

00:11:05.770 --> 00:11:06.150
Got it?

00:11:06.610 --> 00:11:06.960
Yes, ma'am!
Yes, ma'am!

00:11:07.880 --> 00:11:10.200
The sortie will take place in one hour, just as scheduled.

00:11:10.950 --> 00:11:13.150
Commander, will the Infinity be ready in time?

00:11:13.640 --> 00:11:14.850
We'll get it ready in time.

00:11:15.580 --> 00:11:17.170
We'll do the briefing over here.

00:11:17.690 --> 00:11:19.220
Gather here in 30 minutes.

00:11:19.480 --> 00:11:19.910
Roger.

00:11:20.460 --> 00:11:21.450
We'll do everything we can.

00:11:33.160 --> 00:11:35.120
Wow... Amazing.

00:11:35.790 --> 00:11:36.540
Huh? What is?

00:11:36.740 --> 00:11:40.410
There's one person doing all the work to attach the generators to Infi.

00:11:40.470 --> 00:11:40.790
What?

00:11:41.890 --> 00:11:46.050
He's controlling ten Biancas and working the manipulators.

00:11:47.150 --> 00:11:47.590
That's right.

00:11:48.310 --> 00:11:50.420
He's a man who's able to operate 20 Biancas...

00:11:50.620 --> 00:11:52.760
...and use them to do manipulator work.

00:11:52.880 --> 00:11:54.060
Whoa...

00:11:54.530 --> 00:11:56.670
Don't stand there being impressed. Continue configuring the settings!

00:11:56.980 --> 00:11:57.680
Roger!

00:11:59.470 --> 00:12:00.980
Juno, can you hurry a bit more?

00:12:01.320 --> 00:12:02.020
Hmm...

00:12:02.680 --> 00:12:05.370
For now, I'll try to increase my speed by 10%.

00:12:05.600 --> 00:12:06.010
Please do.

00:12:06.350 --> 00:12:07.860
Sure, sure.

00:12:12.170 --> 00:12:14.220
As an added bonus, it's up 20%.

00:12:35.180 --> 00:12:36.540
I don't want to say this...

00:12:37.380 --> 00:12:38.710
...but is Ayaka going to be able to work?

00:12:39.550 --> 00:12:40.850
I'd like to believe so...

00:12:41.460 --> 00:12:42.760
Are you feeling doubtful?

00:12:45.250 --> 00:12:47.030
This isn't training...

00:12:53.000 --> 00:12:54.380
Is this all right?

00:12:56.060 --> 00:12:57.300
Yeah, okay!

00:12:59.940 --> 00:13:00.770
What's the situation?

00:13:02.080 --> 00:13:04.300
The rescue mission will be starting real soon.

00:13:04.790 --> 00:13:05.860
It's all right.

00:13:06.500 --> 00:13:07.370
Let's believe in them.

00:13:08.090 --> 00:13:08.990
You're right...

00:13:09.940 --> 00:13:12.110
Now please rest your body.

00:13:18.380 --> 00:13:19.220
Finished.

00:13:29.520 --> 00:13:30.440
What's going on?

00:13:30.820 --> 00:13:31.480
It's...

00:13:32.900 --> 00:13:34.460
All of the functions are coming back on-line!

00:13:35.240 --> 00:13:36.460
We can open the hangar, too!

00:13:37.500 --> 00:13:39.610
Are they telling us to run?

00:13:43.510 --> 00:13:46.780
As you know, your teacher is a member of the elite.

00:13:47.390 --> 00:13:50.080
She took the initiative and changed jobs at the construction site.

00:13:51.350 --> 00:13:54.910
There were a lot of rumors of her demotion and why she was sent there.

00:13:55.860 --> 00:13:59.190
Even I asked her, "What's someone so elite doing in a place like this?"

00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:01.670
And when I did, she answered like this:

00:14:02.540 --> 00:14:04.560
"I'm doing this because I want to do it."

00:14:11.100 --> 00:14:13.150
The Ultima is suddenly accelerating! It's moving!

00:14:13.500 --> 00:14:14.680
Its purpose is unknown!

00:14:34.320 --> 00:14:35.970
The Ultima's acceleration is not stopping.

00:14:36.170 --> 00:14:37.380
Opening the launch gates.

00:14:37.790 --> 00:14:40.070
I can't believe they would do this 30 minutes before we launch.

00:14:40.590 --> 00:14:42.530
This is another form of ambush.

00:14:43.430 --> 00:14:44.150
What's the status?

00:14:44.560 --> 00:14:46.010
We're still in the middle of configuring the settings.

00:14:46.720 --> 00:14:48.890
But we should be able to somehow maintain an effective speed.

00:14:49.410 --> 00:14:51.410
Sorry. I'm counting on you.

00:14:51.900 --> 00:14:52.390
Yes, sir!
Yes, sir!

00:15:02.200 --> 00:15:03.670
If we set it to full throttle...

00:15:03.960 --> 00:15:05.350
...it looks like it will accelerate suddenly.

00:15:05.640 --> 00:15:06.260
I understand.

00:15:06.850 --> 00:15:07.300
I'll be careful.

00:15:07.690 --> 00:15:08.040
Okay.

00:15:21.400 --> 00:15:24.080
The purpose of this mission is to save people's lives.

00:15:24.630 --> 00:15:26.040
It caught us by surprise...

00:15:26.120 --> 00:15:30.290
...but the enemy leaving the Ultima is good for us.

00:15:31.230 --> 00:15:33.340
I want you to use everything you've got to keep the enemy moving.

00:15:35.620 --> 00:15:36.460
Hello!

00:15:37.390 --> 00:15:38.870
I'm happy that we can fly together.

00:15:39.500 --> 00:15:41.410
Miss Machida, let's do our best.

00:15:42.680 --> 00:15:43.520
It's been a long time since I've seen you.

00:15:47.390 --> 00:15:48.260
Same here.

00:15:52.110 --> 00:15:53.380
Get a grip already...

00:15:54.790 --> 00:15:58.060
It looks like those guys are more proactive this time.

00:15:59.070 --> 00:16:00.720
They're coming to attack. Be careful!

00:16:01.070 --> 00:16:01.620
Here we go!

00:16:02.280 --> 00:16:02.570
Right!

00:16:09.430 --> 00:16:09.980
Kent.

00:16:12.000 --> 00:16:14.260
Let me handle the offense.

00:16:15.350 --> 00:16:15.960
Certainly.

00:16:16.830 --> 00:16:17.440
Thank you.

00:16:44.390 --> 00:16:46.700
Let's withdraw one time! At this rate...

00:16:47.050 --> 00:16:49.330
I understand! Let's try a different approach.

00:16:49.530 --> 00:16:50.660
Keep going, just like that!

00:16:51.360 --> 00:16:53.000
We'll draw their attention!

00:16:55.810 --> 00:16:56.830
Listen, Ayaka!

00:16:57.460 --> 00:16:58.410
Let's try it...

00:16:59.020 --> 00:17:00.180
The gravity pocket!

00:17:12.720 --> 00:17:14.550
Charge into a gravity pocket...

00:17:16.890 --> 00:17:17.990
...and accelerate in one burst!

00:17:27.670 --> 00:17:28.200
Now!

00:17:33.540 --> 00:17:35.010
With the chance that Ayaka got for us...

00:17:37.360 --> 00:17:38.170
This time...

00:17:53.580 --> 00:17:54.280
We did it!

00:18:10.040 --> 00:18:11.720
They're withdrawing from the Ultima?

00:18:12.150 --> 00:18:13.540
What's going on?

00:18:14.230 --> 00:18:16.820
This is U-236! U-236!

00:18:17.090 --> 00:18:18.860
We have succeeded in our escape from the Ultima.

00:18:20.160 --> 00:18:21.840
We've confirmed you, U-236.

00:18:22.300 --> 00:18:23.290
Is everyone aboard?

00:18:23.920 --> 00:18:24.610
Yes, everyone is.

00:18:25.330 --> 00:18:26.860
There's no one left on the Ultima.

00:18:27.190 --> 00:18:27.900
Roger!

00:18:28.490 --> 00:18:29.300
The mission's over!

00:18:29.730 --> 00:18:31.670
All units, withdraw from the front as fast as you can!

00:18:32.360 --> 00:18:32.870
Roger!

00:18:33.320 --> 00:18:33.840
Roger!

00:18:34.130 --> 00:18:34.670
Roger!

00:18:45.720 --> 00:18:47.280
It's no use! I can't control it!

00:19:00.030 --> 00:19:00.900
They saw through it?

00:19:37.280 --> 00:19:38.440
The Ultima is...

00:19:49.650 --> 00:19:51.450
The Ultima...

00:19:52.550 --> 00:19:53.360
...has vanished.

00:20:00.760 --> 00:20:01.420
Papa!

00:20:06.280 --> 00:20:07.130
Papa!

00:20:07.440 --> 00:20:08.050
Rinna!

00:20:09.930 --> 00:20:10.910
Papa!

00:20:17.330 --> 00:20:18.630
Welcome back, Ayaka.

00:20:25.110 --> 00:20:25.790
Welcome back.

00:20:27.070 --> 00:20:29.420
Nice to see you all once again.

00:20:43.210 --> 00:20:44.020
I see...

00:20:45.350 --> 00:20:46.620
So you saw it too, Shima-chan?

00:20:47.520 --> 00:20:48.010
Yeah.

00:20:48.910 --> 00:20:51.330
I was certain that it was your vision, Kouta...

00:20:52.230 --> 00:20:53.820
...because it felt similar.

00:20:54.340 --> 00:20:57.030
I've been seeing that since we started the tests.

00:20:57.960 --> 00:21:00.560
Someone's watching us closely...

00:21:03.080 --> 00:21:04.720
It's felt that way the whole time.

00:21:48.030 --> 00:21:54.870
April 22, 2357 Foundation VI, Ultima annihilated

